# .cursorrules

# Application Overview
APPLICATION_NAME: WayPoint
APPLICATION_PURPOSE: A mobile-first SaaS platform for pet grooming businesses to manage appointments, routes, customers, and payments.
TARGET_USERS: Mobile pet groomers who travel to customers' locations
BUSINESS_MODEL: Subscription-based ($49-79/month per business)
MVP_TIMELINE: 2 months for initial release

# Technical Stack 
TECH_STACK:
  - React Native with Expo (SDK 52)
  - Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Functions)
  - Expo Router for navigation
  - React Native Maps for location services
  - Stripe for payment processing
  - Formik and Yup for form handling
  - TypeScript for type safety
  - React Native Reanimated for animations
  - React Native Paper for UI components
  - AsyncStorage for local data persistence
  - React Native Calendars for appointment scheduling

# Project Structure
PROJECT_STRUCTURE:
  - app/ (Expo Router setup)
    - (tabs)/ (Main tab navigation)
    - _layout.tsx (Root layout)
    - utils/ (Utility functions)
  - components/ (UI components)
    - ui/ (Platform-specific UI components)
  - constants/ (App constants)
  - hooks/ (Custom React hooks)
  - assets/ (Images and fonts)
  - scripts/ (Build and utility scripts)

# Key Features (MVP)
PRIORITY_FEATURES:
  1. Authentication system
  2. Customer & pet profiles
  3. Appointment scheduling
  4. Route optimization
  5. Payment processing
  6. Offline data synchronization

# Coding Standards
CODE_STANDARDS:
  - Use TypeScript with proper typing
  - Use functional components with hooks
  - Follow Expo Router patterns
  - Create reusable components
  - Implement proper error handling
  - Support offline functionality using AsyncStorage
  - Use platform-specific components when necessary (.ios.tsx, .android.tsx)
  - Follow ESLint configuration for code quality
  - Use Formik and Yup for form validation

# State Management
STATE_MANAGEMENT:
  - Use React Context for global state when needed
  - Firebase for remote data
  - AsyncStorage for persistent local data
  - React Query (future consideration) for data fetching and caching

# Offline Strategy
OFFLINE_STRATEGY:
  - Use AsyncStorage to cache essential data
  - Queue writes when offline for later synchronization
  - Implement optimistic UI updates
  - Show appropriate offline indicators to users
  - Sync data when connection is restored

# Testing Strategy
TESTING_STRATEGY:
  - Jest for unit testing
  - React Native Testing Library for component testing
  - Manual testing on physical devices
  - Test offline functionality with network conditions

# Deployment
DEPLOYMENT:
  - Use EAS Build for building app binaries
  - EAS Submit for app store submissions
  - Configure production and staging environments
  - Use EAS Update for over-the-air updates